<title>ISRAEL: Bank Leumi Q1 EPS 0.44 shekel vs 0.08.</title>
<headline>Bank Leumi Q1 EPS 0.44 shekel vs 0.08.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Bank Leumi Ltd.</p>
<p>			   (in thousands of shekels exept EPS)</p>
<p>					  Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>Income before doubtful	  893,410    815,296</p>
<p>debt provision</p>
<p>Doubtful debt provision	 170,343     81,193</p>
<p>Operating, other income</p>
<p>Net income			  618,282    110,939</p>
<p>Earning per share		    0.44	 0.08</p>
<p>Note: First-quarter net income includes a net gain of 456.2 million shekels, from the sale of holdings in Leumi Insurance Holdings and Africa Israel Investments. Net profit from ordinary operations was 162.3 million shekels.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.39 shekels)</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233</p>
</text>
